(def thread-page "(defrule ->>)\n\nNo documentation.")
(def sum-page "(defn sum (values))\n\nAdds the items of an iterator from left to right.\n\nAn empty iterator gives 0. An overflow panics in a debug build, as `add`\ndoes. A vector passes and yields copies of its numbers. `(iter items)` is an\nerror, as its items are borrows, and so is a map.")
(def assoc-page "(defmacro assoc (value key more ...))\n\nReturns a struct or a collection with new values at its keys.\n\nA keyword key sets a field, as in `(assoc point :x 1 :y 2)`. An unknown\nfield is an error, and a keyword without a value is an error. The call moves\neach field it does not list, unless the field is `copy`.\n\nAny other key updates a vector or a map, as in `(assoc items 0 9)`. Keys and\nvalues come in pairs, and each pair updates the result of the one before. A\nmap adds a missing key. A vector panics when an index is out of bounds. The\ncall moves the collection.")
